---
import Base from '../layouts/Base.astro';
import PageFrame from '../components/PageFrame.astro';
import Masthead from '../components/Masthead.astro';
import WorkSection from '../components/WorkSection.astro';
import ActionRow from '../components/ActionRow.astro';
import TextLink from '../components/TextLink.astro';
import Dot from '../components/Dot.astro';
import Figure from '../components/Figure.astro';
import Carousel from '../components/Carousel.astro';
import CaseLead from '../components/CaseLead.astro';
import MetaLine from '../components/MetaLine.astro';
const head = `<link rel="icon" href="data:," />`;
const afterFooter = ``;
---
<Base title={"Design work - Gorka Molero"} description={"These are screens Gorka Molero designed for the Hotpress editor, the Koda desktop app in its four themes and openroadie's interface."} page="design-work">
  <Fragment slot="head" set:html={head} />
  <PageFrame class="sheet">
    <Masthead />

      <CaseLead class="lead">
        <MetaLine class="meta eyebrow">2026 &middot; Product interfaces</MetaLine>
        <h2 class="case-title">Design work</h2>
        <p class="intro">I design what I build. These are screens from Hotpress, Koda and <em>openroadie</em>, with what I decided about the look of each one.</p>
      </CaseLead>

      <main class="systems">
      <WorkSection class="work" id="hotpress">
        <h2><a href="./hotpress.html">Hotpress</a></h2>
        <MetaLine class="meta">Own project &middot; 2026 <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Live at <a href="https://hotpress.app" target="_blank" rel="noopener">hotpress.app</a></MetaLine>
        <p>Hotpress is an app for writing together in real time, with print-ready book and e-book export. The editor screens are frames from a recorded demo of two writers in one document.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/hotpress-style.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/hotpress-style.webp" width="2560" height="850" loading="lazy" alt="The top of hotpress.app: a heavy black rule under the header, a yellow Get Started button with a hard black shadow, and the headline Write together. Publish instantly., with a yellow highlight under its second line." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>I gave Hotpress a neobrutalist look, with 3px black borders, hard 4px shadows with no blur and yellow as the main accent.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/hotpress-pointers.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/hotpress-pointers.webp" width="1824" height="948" loading="lazy" alt="Ana's Hotpress editor, with square avatars for Ana in green and Swift Author in blue, a green LIVE badge, and Swift Author's blue pointer with a name pill." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Each writer keeps one colour across their pointer, name tag, avatar and comment pins.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/hotpress-composer.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/hotpress-composer.webp" width="1920" height="760" loading="lazy" alt="The phrase Light warmed the quay highlighted in yellow, with a New comment composer open under it: a yellow header, a black border and a hard black shadow." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Commenting on a phrase opens the composer right under it, in the same style as the thread.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/hotpress-thread.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/hotpress-thread.webp" width="1920" height="896" loading="lazy" alt="A commented phrase with a pin showing Ana's initial and two comments, and the Discussion popover open beneath it with Ana's comment, Swift Author's reply and a reply box." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>A comment is a pin at the end of the phrase that opens the thread in a popover on the spot, and there's no comments sidebar.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button" href="./hotpress.html">The case study and the video</TextLink>
          <TextLink class="button" href="https://hotpress.app">Open hotpress.app</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work" id="koda">
        <h2><a href="./koda.html">Koda</a></h2>
        <MetaLine class="meta">Own project &middot; 2026 <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Desktop app</MetaLine>
        <p>Koda is a desktop app for working collaboratively with coding agents.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-obsidian.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-obsidian.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="Koda's workspace in Obsidian, its default theme: the ASCII KODA mark over a sidebar of projects, an agent transcript in monospaced type, a permission card outlined in orange, and a file tree with a context meter." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>Koda looks like a terminal, with monospaced type, the KODA mark in ASCII art and actions in brackets, like [SHARE] and [JOIN].</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <p>Obsidian, above, is the default of four themes. Tests check that text meets AA contrast in all four.</p>
        <Carousel class="carousel" aria-label="The same Koda workspace in its other three themes">
          <div class="carousel-track">
            <Figure class="slide"><div class="shot"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-light.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-light.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="Koda's workspace in the Light theme." /></a></div><figcaption>In Light the accent turns blue.</figcaption></Figure>
            <Figure class="slide"><div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-dim.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-dim.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="Koda's workspace in the Dim theme." /></a></div><figcaption>Dim lifts the black a little.</figcaption></Figure>
            <Figure class="slide"><div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-graphite.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-graphite.webp" width="2560" height="1600" loading="lazy" alt="Koda's workspace in the Graphite theme." /></a></div><figcaption>Graphite is blue-grey and keeps the orange.</figcaption></Figure>
          </div>
          <div class="carousel-nav"><button type="button" class="carousel-prev" aria-label="Previous theme">&larr;</button><span class="carousel-count">1 / 3</span><button type="button" class="carousel-next" aria-label="Next theme">&rarr;</button></div>
        </Carousel>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot dark"><a href="./assets/design-work/koda-collaborator.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/design-work/koda-collaborator.webp" width="2560" height="2000" loading="lazy" alt="A collaborator's view of a shared Koda session: the top bar reads SHARED BY GORKA, VIEW, the SHARE action is dimmed, the permission card's Approve once and Deny buttons are greyed out, and a note says the session is read-only." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>A collaborator with view access sees the session under a badge saying who shared it, and the buttons they can't use stay in place, greyed out.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button" href="./koda.html">The case study</TextLink>
          <TextLink class="button" href="https://gorkamolero.github.io/koda/" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Koda's Storybook</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>

      <WorkSection class="work" id="openroadie">
        <h2><a href="https://github.com/RoadieHQ/openroadie" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><em>openroadie</em></a></h2>
        <MetaLine class="meta"><a href="https://roadie.io" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Roadie</a> &middot; 2026 <Dot class="dot">&middot;</Dot> Open source</MetaLine>
        <p><em>openroadie</em> is the open-source context layer that came out of Roadie, and I designed and built its interfaces. They run on <code>@roadiehq/ui</code>, a design system I co-led.</p>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/openroadie-ui/step-flow.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/openroadie-ui/step-flow.webp" width="866" height="784" loading="lazy" alt="An openroadie data-source pipeline: a Trigger card on an hourly schedule, a GitHub repositories source and a Catalog datastore sink, joined by arrows, with 1,204 objects shown on the connector." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>A data-source pipeline reads from top to bottom, from the trigger to the source and the sink, with the number of objects shown on the line between them.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/openroadie-ui/chain-of-thought-dark.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/openroadie-ui/chain-of-thought-dark.webp" width="1049" height="472" loading="lazy" alt="An agent's chain of thought in the dark theme: searching the catalog for Kubernetes workloads, with two workloads as chips, tracing a deployed commit to its pull request, and resolving the owning team." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>The chain of thought lists each step an agent takes, with an icon for each kind of step and the objects it found as chips.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <Figure class="plate">
          <div class="shot"><a href="./assets/openroadie-ui/tool.webp" target="_blank" rel="noopener"><img src="./assets/openroadie-ui/tool.webp" width="1136" height="851" loading="lazy" alt="A tool call, explore_objects_search, with its JSON input and its JSON result, in the light theme." /></a></div>
          <figcaption>A tool call shows its input and its result as code, and the components work in both light and dark.</figcaption>
        </Figure>
        <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button" href="https://github.com/RoadieHQ/openroadie">The source on GitHub</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </WorkSection>

      <ActionRow class="actions"><TextLink class="button primary" href="./design-systems.html">Design systems</TextLink>
        <TextLink class="button" href="./index.html">Engineering portfolio</TextLink></ActionRow>
      </main>
  </PageFrame>
  <Fragment slot="after-footer" set:html={afterFooter} />
</Base>
